# Keep credentials and local state out of the build context.
#
# The build does not COPY any of these today -- Dockerfile.nuitka names its
# sources explicitly (scripts, docs, requirements.txt). This file exists so
# that stays true by construction rather than by everyone remembering. A
# single `COPY . .` added later would otherwise ship the Ed25519 license
# signing key into every customer image, and whoever holds that key can mint
# licenses for any tier forever.
#
# Excluding them also stops the daemon from ever receiving them.

# Signing / licensing key material -- the highest-value secret we hold
*.hex
*.hex.enc
*.pem
*.key
*.jwk

# Runtime secrets and local credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
webhook_secret.txt
dashboard_password.txt

# Local state: pattern databases, logs, license files, backups
scripts/data/
data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.log
backups/

# VCS, tooling and editor noise
.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
